{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLMXzPcapyVMCaxRzpJ4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is done and the polys test suite finished: 825 passed, 5 failed. Those same 5 tests also fail on the unmodified code, so my change didn't cause them:\n\n- `test_fields.py::test_FracElement___call__`\n- `test_partfrac.py::test_noncommutative_pseudomultivariate`\n- `test_polytools.py::test_factor_noeval`\n- `test_polytools.py::test_poly_matching_consistency`\n- `test_polytools.py::test_issue_5786`\n\nThe change is one edit in `sympy/polys/domains/polynomialring.py`, inside `from_FractionField`. When converting a fraction with a constant denominator back to the polynomial ring, it now uses exact division and declines the conversion if the division leaves a remainder. Before, it used `/`, which silently dropped terms like `a/2` and made `bug.apart(t)` return `-a*t`.\n\nThe issue's example now gives `-a*t + a/2 - a/(2*(2*t - 1))`, and subtracting the original expression and simplifying gives `0`.\n\n`(3*a + 4)/2` in the integer polynomial ring `ZZ[a]` still returns `2`. I left it alone to keep the fix minimal, but other code that relies on it could still give wrong results."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":151,"cache_read_input_tokens":35409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":151},"output_tokens":425,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c6c1ea3-2cbd-4791-a4a3-69ce7b659f94","uuid":"df537240-746e-481a-ab04-d42a122b695c","timestamp":"2026-11-23T18:44:59.836Z","request_id":"req_011ChLMXz32hWLp38xgNmRJg"}
